    <!-- Privacy Policy V2 - authoritative legal copy -->
    <string name="privacy_v2_last_updated" translatable="false">Last updated: August 31, 2026</string>
    <string name="privacy_v2_section_1_title" translatable="false">1. Overview</string>
    <string name="privacy_v2_section_1_content" translatable="false">One Line A Day is designed as a local-first journaling application. Your journal entries, moods, tags, attached media, and voice notes are primarily stored in the app\'s private storage on your device.\n\nWe do not operate our own account or journal-sync server, and your journal content is not intentionally sent to us for advertising or analytics. However, the app uses third-party Google services for advertising and purchases, and those services may process technical device and usage information as described below.</string>
    <string name="privacy_v2_section_2_title" translatable="false">2. Journal Data Stored on Your Device</string>
    <string name="privacy_v2_section_2_content" translatable="false">Journal entries, moods, dates, tags, streak information, and related journal metadata are stored using Android Room and SQLite in the app\'s private storage.\n\nPhotos, videos, and voice recordings that you attach may also be copied into private application storage.\n\nThe application does not currently add its own database-level encryption layer to the Room database. Your device and Android operating system may provide storage encryption and other device-level protections. You can also enable App Lock inside One Line A Day to require device authentication before opening the diary.</string>
    <string name="privacy_v2_section_3_title" translatable="false">3. Advertising and Google Services</string>
    <string name="privacy_v2_section_3_content" translatable="false">One Line A Day uses Google Mobile Ads to display advertising, including banner, native, interstitial, and rewarded advertisements.\n\nGoogle Mobile Ads may collect or share technical information such as IP address, approximate location derived from IP address, app interactions, diagnostic information, and device or advertising identifiers. This information may be used for advertising, analytics, fraud prevention, security, and related Google services.\n\nYour journal text, journal photos, tags, and voice recordings are not intentionally supplied to Google Mobile Ads for advertising.\n\nThe app also uses Google Play Billing for optional premium purchases. Purchase processing is handled by Google Play. The app may receive purchase and entitlement information needed to determine whether premium features are available. We do not receive your full payment-card information.</string>
    <string name="privacy_v2_section_4_title" translatable="false">4. Device Permissions</string>
    <string name="privacy_v2_section_4_content" translatable="false">Notifications: Used to provide optional daily journal reminders.\n\nMicrophone: Used only when you choose to record a voice note.\n\nReceive Boot Completed: Used to restore scheduled reminder notifications after the device restarts.\n\nBiometric authentication: Used when you enable App Lock so Android can authenticate you using supported device security such as biometrics, PIN, pattern, or password.\n\nInternet and network state: Required by features such as Google Mobile Ads and Google Play services.\n\nThe app does not request general location, contacts, SMS, call log, or broad external-storage permissions.</string>
    <string name="privacy_v2_section_5_title" translatable="false">5. Backup, Export and Sharing</string>
    <string name="privacy_v2_section_5_content" translatable="false">One Line A Day disables Android automatic app backup (allowBackup=false) for journal data in the current release to protect journal privacy. If you use user-initiated export features such as PDF or ZIP backup and choose another application or cloud-storage provider, that exported data will be handled by the destination you select and according to that provider\'s privacy practices.\n\nWe do not automatically upload your journal entries to our own cloud server.</string>
    <string name="privacy_v2_section_6_title" translatable="false">6. Security</string>
    <string name="privacy_v2_section_6_content" translatable="false">Journal data is stored within Android application-private storage. The app also provides an optional App Lock that uses Android device authentication.\n\nNo application or security system can guarantee absolute security. You should keep your Android device protected with a PIN, password, pattern, or supported biometric authentication and keep the operating system updated.</string>
    <string name="privacy_v2_section_7_title" translatable="false">7. Children\'s Privacy</string>
    <string name="privacy_v2_section_7_content" translatable="false">One Line A Day is not specifically designed as a service directed at children. We do not claim that the application is automatically compliant with every child-privacy law in every country.\n\nIf the application is distributed to audiences that include children, additional Google Play Families, advertising, consent, and regional legal requirements may apply.</string>
    <string name="privacy_v2_section_8_title" translatable="false">8. Contact and Policy Updates</string>
    <string name="privacy_v2_section_8_content" translatable="false">We may update this Privacy Policy when the application, third-party SDKs, legal requirements, or data practices change.\n\nFor privacy questions or concerns, contact:\n\ndeveloperaisteps@gmail.com</string>

